WEBVTT

NOTE
Descriptive captions for JPL's Rover Mission Animation (6 June 2003).
This 90-second educational montage shows the prelaunch mission plan, not real mission footage.
Original soundtrack removed: music ownership is not identified.
Video courtesy NASA/JPL-Caltech. Animation: Dan Maas. Technical consultant: Steve Squyres.
Embedded source copyright: 2002 Cornell University. Educational reuse under JPL Image Use Policy.

00:00.000 --> 00:05.000
In June 2003, NASA shared this animation of the plan.

00:05.000 --> 00:13.000
A Delta rocket lifts the Mars Exploration Rover toward space.

00:13.000 --> 00:20.000
The spacecraft cruises away from Earth toward Mars.

00:20.000 --> 00:28.000
The heat shield protects it as it enters Mars' atmosphere.

00:28.000 --> 00:34.000
A parachute opens to slow the spacecraft.

00:34.000 --> 00:37.000
The heat shield falls away.

00:37.000 --> 00:41.000
The lander hangs below the parachute on a long tether.

00:41.000 --> 00:46.000
Airbags inflate around the lander.

00:46.000 --> 00:52.000
Rockets slow the fall before the tether is cut.

00:52.000 --> 01:00.000
The airbag-covered lander bounces across the Martian ground.

01:00.000 --> 01:04.000
The airbags pull back.

01:04.000 --> 01:10.000
The lander opens its petals.

01:10.000 --> 01:22.000
The rover drives down onto Mars.

01:22.000 --> 01:30.000
Its robot arm reaches out to explore a rock.
